-- title:
--   Non-smooth closed fibre of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K$ carry a compatible $A$-algebra structure (scalar tower $A \to L \to K$). Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ equal to the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series numerator of the classical $j$-invariant. Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) for the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras `chartAlg A K {j}` and `chartAlg A K {j⁻¹}` of $K$, and [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) for the morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ descended from the two structure morphisms. The assertion is: for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : A \to k$ that is not injective, the second projection of the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi)$ is not smooth.
--
--   The geometric fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the closed point of the discrete valuation ring $A$ is singular: its two branches cross at the supersingular points, so the fibre is not smooth over the residue field. This negative smoothness statement is what allows the theorems on the special fibre of the model of $X_1(Mp)$ — its connectedness, the description of the minimal primes of the fibre, and the identification of the crossing points with supersingular $j$-invariants — to be applied in the form they require.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_not_smooth_pullback_snd_modelTo_of_not_injective_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

